    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i used to think i was special. like, i actually believed i had that spark for competitive programming. but after this last set of results... it finally hit me. i'm just a mid-tier dev. i'll never be one of the ones people actually remember. i'm just gonna spend the next 40 years being \"fine\" and \"competent\" while the real geniuses move the world. it feels like a joke.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'm really sorry that you're feeling this way. Please remember that struggling and facing challenges is a part of every journey, and your worth is not defined solely by your achievements in competitive programming or any one area. Competitiveness and creativity are skills that everyone can develop with dedication and time. Your \"fine\" and \"competent\" qualities are still valuable, and there are always opportunities to keep growing. Don't write off your potential too soon.",
